      'gdrive.title': 'Back up to your Google Drive', 'gdrive.console': 'Open Google Cloud Console',
      'gdrive.intro': 'Your data lives in this browser only. One bad day \u2014 a cleared cache, a lost iPad \u2014 and it is gone. A backup in your own Google Drive takes a minute and costs nothing.',
      'gdrive.s1': 'Press <b>Export Backup</b> under Data & Sync. One JSON file is downloaded with every player, match, drill, tactic and recorded clip in it.',
      'gdrive.s2': 'Open <b>drive.google.com</b> and drag the file into a folder \u2014 make one called <b>SportTactic</b> so it is easy to find.',
      'gdrive.s3': 'Do it again after every match weekend. Keep the last three files; the name already carries the date.',
      'gdrive.s4': 'To put a backup back: Data & Sync \u2192 <b>Import Backup</b> \u2192 pick the JSON file from Drive.',
      'gdrive.s5': 'Right-click the file in Drive \u2192 Share, to give an assistant coach a copy.',
      'gdrive.autoTitle': 'Or let the app do it',
      'gdrive.a1': 'Open Google Cloud Console \u2192 <b>Credentials</b> \u2192 Create credentials \u2192 <b>OAuth client ID</b> \u2192 Web application.',
      'gdrive.a2': 'Add this site\u2019s address as an <b>authorised JavaScript origin</b> and save.',
      'gdrive.a3': 'Copy the Client ID into the field above.',
      'gdrive.a4': 'Press <b>Back up to Drive</b>. You sign in with Google once, and the file is written to <b>/SportTactic/sporttactic-backup.json</b> in your own Drive.',
      'gdrive.tail': 'The app talks to Google directly from your device. Nothing passes through a SportTactic server, and no one else can read the file unless you share it.',

      'oauth.title': 'How to get a Google OAuth Client ID',
      'oauth.intro': 'A Client ID is the name tag SportTactic shows Google so it may ask <b>you</b> for permission to write one backup file into <b>your</b> Drive. It is not a password and it is not secret \u2014 it only works from this exact web address.',
      'oauth.free': 'It is free, takes about five minutes, and you only do it once. Skip it entirely if you would rather just download the backup and drag it into Drive yourself.',
      'oauth.stepsTitle': 'Step by step',
      'oauth.s1': 'Go to <b>console.cloud.google.com</b> and sign in with the Google account that should own the backups.',
      'oauth.s2': 'Top bar \u2192 the project picker \u2192 <b>New project</b>. Call it <b>SportTactic</b> and create it. Make sure it is the selected project afterwards.',
      'oauth.s3': 'Left menu \u2192 <b>APIs & Services</b> \u2192 <b>Library</b>. Search for <b>Google Drive API</b> and press <b>Enable</b>.',
      'oauth.s4': '<b>APIs & Services</b> \u2192 <b>OAuth consent screen</b>. Choose <b>External</b>, fill in an app name and your own e-mail twice, and save through to the end.',
      'oauth.s5': 'Still on the consent screen, add your own Google address under <b>Test users</b>. Without this Google will refuse to sign you in.',
      'oauth.s6': '<b>Credentials</b> \u2192 <b>Create credentials</b> \u2192 <b>OAuth client ID</b> \u2192 Application type <b>Web application</b>.',
      'oauth.s7': 'Under <b>Authorised JavaScript origins</b> press Add URI and paste the address shown below. Leave <b>Authorised redirect URIs</b> empty \u2014 this app does not use one.',
      'oauth.s8': 'Press <b>Create</b> and copy the <b>Client ID</b> (it ends in <b>.apps.googleusercontent.com</b>). Paste it into the field above. You never need the client secret.',
      'oauth.originTitle': 'The address to paste into Google',
      'oauth.originHint': 'This is exactly what SportTactic is running on right now. It must match character for character \u2014 no path, no trailing slash. If you later move the app to another address, add that one too.',
      'oauth.copy': 'Copy', 'oauth.copied': 'Address copied',
      'oauth.troubleTitle': 'If Google complains',
      'oauth.t1': '<b>origin_mismatch</b> or "not allowed": the address above is not in Authorised JavaScript origins, or it differs by http/https, port or a trailing slash.',
      'oauth.t2': '<b>access_denied</b>: your own e-mail is not listed under Test users on the consent screen.',
      'oauth.t3': '<b>Google hasn\u2019t verified this app</b>: that is expected for a private project \u2014 press <b>Advanced</b> and then continue. Verification is only needed to publish to strangers.',
      'oauth.t4': 'Nothing happens at all: the browser blocked the Google sign-in pop-up. Allow pop-ups for this site and try again.',
      'oauth.privacy': 'The Client ID stays in your own settings on this device. SportTactic asks Google for permission from your browser only \u2014 no server of ours ever sees your Drive or your files.',

      'sheets.title': 'Use Google Sheets as your database', 'sheets.open': 'Create a new Google Sheet',
      'sheets.intro': 'You do not need a server to keep your squad in a spreadsheet. SportTactic writes plain CSV, and Google Sheets reads it \u2014 that is the whole trick.',
      'sheets.s1': 'Press <b>Export squad as CSV</b> above. The file lands in your downloads.',
      'sheets.s2': 'Open <b>sheets.new</b> to make an empty sheet, then <b>File \u2192 Import \u2192 Upload</b> and drop the CSV in. Choose <i>Replace current sheet</i>.',
      'sheets.s3': 'You now have the squad as a real spreadsheet \u2014 sort it, chart it, share it with the board, print it for the bus.',
      'sheets.s4': 'Edit it in Sheets when it is easier there, then <b>File \u2192 Download \u2192 Comma-separated values</b> to get the CSV back.',
      'sheets.s5': 'Reports have their own CSV button, so match statistics go the same way.',
      'sheets.s6': 'For everything at once \u2014 matches, drills, tactics \u2014 use the JSON backup instead; a spreadsheet cannot hold video clips.',
      'sheets.tail': 'Sheets is the copy you show people; SportTactic stays the copy you work in. Re-import a CSV only when you really mean to overwrite what is on the device.',
      'drive.title': 'Google Drive Sync', 'drive.hint': 'Back up and sync your data to your own Google Drive. Paste an OAuth Client ID (Web app) from Google Cloud Console whose authorised JavaScript origin is this site.',
